  "NT:mwb06a6oiyyg": {
   "x": 93.5,
   "y": 922.5,
   "w": 392,
   "h": 329,
   "html": "<h3 class=\"ph\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 0.7; text-wrap: wrap;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 16px; font-family: var(--body);\">I studied \"Synergetics\" in greater depth in 1984, and became fascinated with his theoretical argument that the traditional X, Y, Z Cartesian coordinate system distorted our understanding of reality. He argued that everything that was alive and existed in Nature, from sub-atomic particals to cosmological structures, whether alive or not, did so based on polyhedral geometry. And that the Tetrahedron was a fundamental form at all scales. He believed that the face-bonded \"Tetra-Helix\", was a special case, an extension of a single tetrahedron that he believed could explain the structure of DNA. At the time of my reading of Synergetics in 1985, other theories prevailed, but still I felt there might be a connection somehow.&nbsp;</span></h3><h3 class=\"ph\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 0.7; text-wrap: wrap;\"><br></h3>",
   "z": 950,
   "new": "text",
   "t": 1794348183907
  },
