  "T:AwakeningArtwork": {
   "x": 101,
   "y": -40,
   "w": 771.5,
   "h": 200,
   "html": "<h3 class=\"ph\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 0.7; text-wrap: wrap;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: var(--body);\">In the months preceding the Kundalini awakening I was working intensely to create an \"Artist's Portfolio\" for my applications to architecture schools. Most of the artwork I had done up to this point was the typical technical school level technical drafting of floor plans and elevations. So I started drawing scenes of objects to came to mind or landscapes &amp; natural objects with a focus of 3-Dimensionality and realism. I also had taken some anatomical drawing classes with a teacher that emphasized classical anatomy and \"seeing into space\". Some of these are from those classes, most are simply imagined fantasies of the human form.</span></h3>",
   "t": 1794410355657
  },
